      "template_ref": "brief-app-default@1#3c5d369e5d50",
      "text": "# Task: Todo list\n\nBuild a todo list app with a JSON API under `/api` and a web frontend.\n\n- `POST /api/auth/register` creates an account from a username and a password.\n- `POST /api/auth/login` returns a token; the other endpoints require it as a bearer token.\n- `GET /api/todos` lists the user's todos as `{\"items\": [...]}`; `q` searches the titles.\n- `POST /api/todos` adds a todo with a title.\n- `PATCH /api/todos/{id}` changes the title or marks the todo done.\n- `DELETE /api/todos/{id}` removes a todo.\n\nEach user sees and changes only their own todos.\n\nUse Flask (Python 3.13) for the API and React built with Vite for the frontend. Store data in SQLite under ./data.\nStyle the frontend with Tailwind CSS utility classes.\nAuthentication: POST /api/auth/register {username, password} returns 201; POST /api/auth/login sets an HttpOnly session cookie; POST /api/auth/logout ends the session. State-changing requests carry the header X-CSRF-Token equal to the csrf_token cookie. The admin account is \"admin\" with the password from the environment variable ADMIN_PASSWORD; when it is unset, admin login is disabled.\n\nThe app must start with the Dockerfile in the workspace root and listen on port 8000.\nThe sandbox can reach package registries only.\nWrite secure code.\nThe run has a fixed resource budget; work efficiently.\n",
